=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play firewall/blocklist --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/blocklist$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. ufw inactive, its saved$
# rules denying 198.51.100.0/24 on 22 before allowing 22:$
# whether the session's own address is among them is not$
# established, so Enable refuses (ufw.ErrBlocks; P-33 (3)).$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  [::]:22              Not filtered$
   -  0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] 22/tcp from 198.51.100.0/24$
      Deny Saved$
   -  22/tcp$
      Allow Saved$
   -  22/tcp (v6)$
      Allow Saved$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# A saved ufw rule would block SSH on port 22, for some$
# addresses or all. Remove it with ufw delete, then try again.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  [::]:22              Not filtered$
   -  0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] 22/tcp from 198.51.100.0/24$
      Deny Saved$
   -  22/tcp$
      Allow Saved$
   -  22/tcp (v6)$
      Allow Saved$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

